  "translations": {
    "translations": [
      {
        "iso_3166_1": "FR",
        "iso_639_1": "fr",
        "name": "Français",
        "english_name": "French",
        "data": {
          "homepage": "https://www.france.tv/france-5/le-monde-en-face/8126115-iran-israel-et-la-bombe.html",
          "overview": "Les services de renseignement israéliens mènent depuis les années 2000 une série d’opérations clandestines en Iran — cambriolages, piratages, assassinats — pour freiner le programme nucléaire militaire de Téhéran. L’Iran finance parallèlement des milices hostiles à Israël, comme le Hamas ou le Hezbollah. Israël juge que la République islamique approche du seuil nucléaire et, le 13 juin 2025, la guerre secrète bascule en affrontement ouvert, jusqu’à l’intervention de l’aviation américaine et la destruction de sites nucléaires souterrains iraniens.  Le documentaire de Miyuki Droz et Sylvain Lepetit retrace ces vingt ans d’espionnage grâce à des témoignages d’anciens responsables israéliens et iraniens. Animations et images immersives dévoilent les opérations des commandos et l’intérieur des centrales, mêlant récit d’action et analyse géopolitique du Moyen-Orient.",
          "runtime": 77,
          "tagline": "",
          "title": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "iso_3166_1": "SE",
        "iso_639_1": "sv",
        "name": "svenska",
        "english_name": "Swedish",
        "data": {
          "homepage": "",
          "overview": "Lönnmord, spioneri och cyberattacker. Israel har inte skytt några medel under de 20 år landet har försökt förhindra att Iran utvecklar kärnvapen. Attackerna kulminerade 2025 då Israel och USA bombade landets kärnanläggningar. Nya bombningar inleds i februari 2026, nu för att störta regimen i Teheran. Frågan kvarstår: har Iran kärnvapen eller inte?",
          "runtime": 51,
          "tagline": "",
          "title": "Iran, Israel och kärnvapnen"
        }
      },
      {
        "iso_3166_1": "US",
        "iso_639_1": "en",
        "name": "English",
        "english_name": "English",
        "data": {
          "homepage": "https://javafilms.fr/film/iran-israel-and-the-bomb/",
          "overview": "On February 28, 2026, the US and Israel launched massive strikes on Iran, claiming an imminent nuclear threat.  This film traces how the world reached this point after more than three decades of shadow war over “the bomb”.  Israel has tried to block Tehran’s nuclear drive with sabotage, assassinations and cyberwar – from the Stuxnet virus wrecking Natanz centrifuges to the AI-assisted killing of nuclear programme “father” Mohsen Fakhrizadeh, and a commando raid stealing 1.5 tonnes of secret nuclear archive files.  Iran insists uranium enrichment is its sovereign right and key to national identity and regional power.  As Israel pounded Iran’s nuclear facilities in June 2025 and systematically weakened its allies in Gaza, Lebanon, Syria and Yemen, nuclear talks continued in Geneva. Iran was edging towards diluting weapons-grade uranium – but Israel wasn’t prepared to wait, and pulled Washington into open war whose global consequences are only now beginning to unfold.",
          "runtime": 54,
          "tagline": "What led to the war?",
          "title": "Iran, Israel and the Bomb"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
